from h34 import *
M=mcq;F=tf;S=short;N=num
chapter(4,'english','the-old-stag','The Old Stag',
 ('A kind stag and a hillock of grass','An old stag lives in a lush forest and is loved by all the animals. When he falls ill and rests on his hillock of tender grass, his visitors eat the grass until none is left for him. This Panchatantra story teaches us to use nature\'s resources wisely. In this chapter you will read the story, learn descriptive words and adverbs of manner, write about a friend and think about sharing.'),
 [('The kind stag',['In a lush forest lived an old stag who was known for his kindness. Each day he warmly greeted his fellow animals and birds.','Although the forest had plenty of food, the stag liked to stay on a small hillock covered with soft, tender grass.','Every day he came down to meet his friends, and all the animals and birds loved him.']),
  ('The stag falls ill',['One day the stag fell ill and struggled to reach the hillock.','He knew that fresh healthy food and proper rest would help him get well, so he ate the tender grass and rested.','He could not go down to greet his friends, and they became worried and came to check on him.','The deer, elephant and giraffe wished him a speedy recovery.']),
  ('The grass disappears',['Before leaving, the visitors ate some of the fresh green grass on the hillock and said how tender and juicy it was.','Word spread, and every animal who came to visit the stag also feasted on the grass.','Soon there was hardly any grass left for the stag, and he grew weaker day by day.','Greed had made his friends forget the very friend they had come to help.']),
  ('The animals learn',['His friends felt ashamed when they realised their mistake.','They decided to find food elsewhere in the forest and not disturb the hillock, and some brought fresh leaves for him.','That week it rained well, the grass grew back, and slowly the stag recovered.','The lesson of this Panchatantra tale is that nature has enough for everybody, but we need to use its resources wisely.']),
  ('New words and meanings',['Lush means green and thick, like a lush forest. Tender means soft and young, like tender grass.','A hillock is a small hill. A stag is a male deer. Recovery is getting well again, and a speedy recovery is quick healing.','A shaded spot is a cool resting place. Healthy food is wholesome food that nourishes us.']),
  ('Descriptive words and adverbs',['Describing words like lush forest, friendly animals and tender grass give more detail and make writing interesting.','An adverb of manner tells how something is done. Warmly greeted tells how the stag greeted. Slowly recovered tells how he recovered.','Quietly, cheerfully, carefully, loudly, fast and badly are adverbs of manner.','Soon, early and lately tell when, and nearby tells where, so they are not adverbs of manner.']),
  ('Writing and speaking',['In The Monkeys\' Fast, monkeys decide to fast till sunset, but they cannot resist peeling bananas and taking just one bite, so they learn that fasting needs self-control.','To write about a best friend use pronouns: she or he, her or his. My best friend is Anu. She is eight years old. Her hobby is drawing.','Imagine a bowl of jalebis shared in class. If everyone keeps taking more, some friends get none, so we should share and take only our turn.','You can make a thank you card from the old stag to his friends for the leaves and the care.'])],
 [('Pick the adverb of manner: The rabbit quickly ate the carrots.',[('Ask how the rabbit ate.','Adverbs of manner tell how.'),('It ate quickly.','Quickly describes the eating.'),('So quickly is the adverb.','It ends in -ly, which is common for adverbs of manner.')]),
  ('Match: speedy recovery means ___.',[('Recovery means getting well.','Speedy means quick.'),('So speedy recovery means quick healing.','It is a kind wish for someone who is ill.')])],
 ('Tell the story of the old stag and explain its lesson.',['The stag stayed on the hillock with tender grass','He fell ill and the visitors ate the grass','The animals felt ashamed and found food elsewhere','Use nature wisely, there is enough for everyone'],['The stag was angry with the animals','The forest had no other food']),
 ['The old stag was kind and loved by all.','The visitors ate the grass and left none for the sick stag.','They found food elsewhere and the grass grew back.','Adverbs of manner tell how something is done.','Nature has enough for everybody if we use it wisely.'],
 [M('1',1,'Why was the old stag popular?','He was kind and greeted everyone',[('He was strong','The story says kindness'),('He had food for all','The story says kindness')],'All the animals loved him.'),
  M('2',1,'Why could the stag not go down the hillock?','He was ill and weak',[('He was lazy','He was ill'),('He was afraid','He was ill')],'He struggled even to reach the hillock.'),
  M('3',1,'Why did the green cover of the hillock vanish?','The visiting animals ate the grass',[('The sun burnt it','The animals ate it'),('The stag ate it all','Visitors ate it')],'Everyone who visited ate some.'),
  M('4',1,'What did the animals do when they realised their mistake?','Found food elsewhere and brought leaves',[('Left the stag','They helped him'),('Ate more grass','They stopped eating it')],'They stopped disturbing the hillock.'),
  M('5',2,'What does lush mean?','Green and thick',[('Dry','The opposite'),('Tiny','Not the meaning')],'A lush forest is full of green plants.'),
  M('6',2,'What does tender grass mean?','Soft young grass',[('Sharp grass','Tender is soft'),('Dead grass','Tender is young')],'Tender means soft and delicate.'),
  M('7',2,'What is a hillock?','A small hill',[('A big mountain','Hillock is small'),('A river','Not a hill')],'A hillock is a little hill.'),
  M('8',2,'Which is an adverb of manner?','Carefully',[('Nearby','Nearby tells where'),('Early','Early tells when')],'Carefully tells how something is done.'),
  M('9',2,'Which word describes how the stag greeted?','warmly',[('daily','Not how'),('forest','Not an adverb')],'He warmly greeted them.'),
  F('10',2,'The forest had no food except the grass on the hillock.',False,'The forest had plenty of food.'),
  S('11',2,'Which book is the story adapted from?',['panchatantra','the panchatantra'],'It is adapted from the Panchatantra.'),
  M('12',3,'What is the lesson of the story?','Nature has enough for everybody if used wisely',[('Never visit a sick friend','Visiting is good'),('Grass is tasty','Not the lesson')],'We must use resources wisely and not be greedy.')],
 keep=['hillock','stag'])
